# Graphs in the UI: `open_graph`, `propose_graph`, the graph preview dialog and `?node=` (KAN-91 #2, #8)

## What to build

Two agent tools that show a task graph on the user's screen, plus the server and web pieces they need:

1. **`GET /api/workspaces/:id/graph?tasksDir=…`** → `{ nodes, edges, layers }` of a task folder, built from its task files exactly like a run's graph (`buildGraph`/`layersOf` in `src/server/runs.ts`), every node with status `pending`.
2. **`open_graph { runId?, tasksDir?, node? }`** (exactly one of `runId`/`tasksDir`; `node` must exist) → queues `{ kind: "open-graph", runId?, tasksDir?, node? }`. The web opens `/runs/:ws/:runId?node=<id>` for a run, or a read-only **graph preview dialog** for a folder.
3. **`propose_graph { tasksDir, spec, provider?, options? }`** (validated like `open_start_run`) → queues `{ kind: "propose-graph", prefill }`. The web shows the same dialog with **Approve** / **Reject**. Approve opens the prefilled Start run drawer (which then sends `originTerminalId`); Reject acks with `{ result: "rejected" }` and the server types `[graph-manager] The user rejected the graph <tasksDir>.` into the calling terminal.
4. **`POST /api/agent-requests/:id/ack`** accepts an optional body `{ result?: "approved" | "rejected" }`.
5. **`RunDetail`** reads `?node=<id>`, selects that node and scrolls it into view.
6. **`StartRunDrawer`** gets an `originTerminalId` prop and sends it in `POST /api/runs/:ws` (for `start-run` requests and approved `propose-graph` requests).

Spec: `docs/prd/agent-supervisor.md` (tool rows `open_graph`, `propose_graph`; "Agent requests and the web"; Decisions rows on `open_graph` and `propose_graph`).

**Already in the codebase from earlier slices** (read them, don't rebuild them):

- `src/server/agent-requests.ts` exports the discriminated union (server side):
  ```ts
  export interface StartRunPrefill { tasksDir: string; spec: string; provider?: string; options?: RunOptionsBody }
  interface AgentRequestBase { id: string; workspaceId: string; agent?: string; terminalTitle?: string; createdAt: string }
  interface TerminalRequestBase extends AgentRequestBase { terminalId: string }
  export interface StartRunRequest extends TerminalRequestBase { kind: "start-run"; prefill: StartRunPrefill }
  export interface OpenRunRequest extends TerminalRequestBase { kind: "open-run"; runId: string }
  export interface OpenGraphRequest extends TerminalRequestBase { kind: "open-graph"; runId?: string; tasksDir?: string; node?: string }
  export interface ProposeGraphRequest extends TerminalRequestBase { kind: "propose-graph"; prefill: StartRunPrefill }
  export interface RefreshRequest extends AgentRequestBase { kind: "refresh" }
  export type AgentRequest = StartRunRequest | OpenRunRequest | OpenGraphRequest | ProposeGraphRequest | RefreshRequest;
  export type NewAgentRequest<R extends AgentRequest = AgentRequest> = R extends AgentRequest ? Omit<R, "id" | "createdAt"> : never;
  // class AgentRequests: add(r: NewAgentRequest): AgentRequest (replaces a pending one of the same terminal AND kind),
  // list(), get(id): AgentRequest | undefined, ack(id): boolean (false for unknown ids and for refresh requests)
  ```
- `src/web/types.ts` has the same union for the web: `AgentRequestPrefill` (`{ tasksDir; spec; provider?; options?: Record<string, unknown> }`), `StartRunRequest`, `OpenRunRequest`, `OpenGraphRequest`, `ProposeGraphRequest`, `RefreshRequest`, `AgentRequest`, `TerminalAgentRequest = Exclude<AgentRequest, RefreshRequest>`.
- `src/web/agentRequests.tsx`: `requestText(r: TerminalAgentRequest)` already returns `<Agent> in <repo> wants to show you a graph` for `open-graph` and `propose-graph`. `AgentRequestHost` loops over `overview.agentRequests` with a `switch (r.kind)`: `start-run`, `open-run`, `refresh` are handled; `open-graph` and `propose-graph` just `break` — this slice fills those two cases. It has refs `opened`, `toasted`, an `ack(id)` helper and the `visible` terminal set (`VisibleTerminals` context; `visible.has(r.terminalId) && !document.hidden` means "the calling terminal is on screen in this tab").
- `src/server/tools/run-helpers.ts`: `requireWorkspace(tc): Workspace | ToolResult` (error `this terminal is not inside a graph-manager workspace`), `runDirOrError(ws, runId): Promise<string | ToolResult>` (error `unknown run <id>`), `isToolResult(x)`.
- `src/server/terminals.ts`: `TerminalManager.typeWhenIdle(id: string, line: string): boolean` — queues one line to type into an agent terminal once it is quiet (false when the terminal is unknown or not an agent terminal). Reach it as `ctx.terminals.typeWhenIdle`.
- `src/server/routes/runs.ts` `startBody` accepts an optional `originTerminalId: string` and records the run's origin.

