## Patterns to follow

**Folder graph (runs.ts)** — split `graphOf` so the task-file half is reusable, then:
```ts
/** The graph of a task folder's files, every node `pending`; undefined when the folder can't be read. */
export async function folderGraph(tasksDir: string): Promise<RunGraph | undefined> {
  const tasks = await readTasks(tasksDir);
  return tasks ? tasksGraph(tasks, () => "pending").graph : undefined;
}
```
where `tasksGraph(tasks: TaskFile[], statusOf: (id: string) => string): { graph: RunGraph; deps: Map<string, string[]> }` is the existing second half of `graphOf` (sorted by `byId`, deps filtered to known ids, edges `[dep, id]`, `layersOf`), and `graphOf` calls it for the non-empty case. Behaviour of `buildGraph`/`runDetail` must not change.

**Route (inspect.ts)**:
```ts
app.get<{ Params: { id: string }; Querystring: { tasksDir?: string } }>("/api/workspaces/:id/graph", async (req, reply) => {
  const ws = resolveWorkspace(ctx.config.workspacesDir, req.params.id);
  if (!ws) return reply.code(404).send({ error: "unknown workspace" });
  const rel = typeof req.query.tasksDir === "string" ? req.query.tasksDir : "";
  if (rel === "") return reply.code(400).send({ error: "tasksDir is required" });
  const full = insideWorkspace(ws, rel);
  const graph = full ? await folderGraph(full) : undefined;
  if (!graph || graph.nodes.length === 0) return reply.code(404).send({ error: `no task files in ${rel}` });
  return graph;
});
```

**Tool error/success style** (from `open-start-run.ts`): `{ isError: true, text: "…" }`, nothing queued on error. Export `resolveIn` from `open-start-run.ts` (rename nothing) and import it in the new tools.

**Ack route with a body**:
```ts
const ackBody = z.object({ result: z.enum(["approved", "rejected"]).optional() });
app.post<{ Params: { id: string } }>("/api/agent-requests/:id/ack", async (req, reply) => {
  const parsed = ackBody.safeParse(req.body ?? {});
  if (!parsed.success) return reply.code(400).send({ error: "result must be approved or rejected" });
  const r = ctx.agentRequests.get(req.params.id);
  if (!r || !ctx.agentRequests.ack(r.id)) return reply.code(404).send({ error: "request not found" });
  if (r.kind === "propose-graph" && parsed.data.result === "rejected")
    ctx.terminals.typeWhenIdle(r.terminalId, `[graph-manager] The user rejected the graph ${r.prefill.tasksDir}.`);
  return reply.code(204).send();
});
```
`post(url)` from the web without a body sends no JSON; `req.body` is then undefined, hence `?? {}`.

**Preview dialog** (new `src/web/pages/GraphPreviewDialog.tsx`), mirroring `ConfirmDialog`'s overlay/focus trap but wide:
```tsx
export function GraphPreviewDialog({ open, workspaceId, tasksDir, node, propose, onClose, onApprove, onReject }: {
  open: boolean; workspaceId: string; tasksDir: string; node?: string;
  /** Approve / Reject buttons (propose_graph); otherwise only Close. */
  propose?: boolean;
  onClose: () => void; onApprove?: () => void; onReject?: () => void;
}) { /* fetch api<RunGraph>(`/api/workspaces/${enc(ws)}/graph?tasksDir=${enc(tasksDir)}`) when open;
        title `Graph of ${tasksDir}`, a subtitle with `workspaceLabel(workspaceId)`; body: <TaskGraph graph={g} selected={node} />
        (scroll `[data-testid="graph-node-<node>"]` into view once loaded), or the API error text, or "Loading…".
        Buttons: propose → "Reject" (data-testid graph-preview-reject) and "Approve" (btn-primary, graph-preview-approve);
        always "Close" (graph-preview-close, Esc). Root data-testid "graph-preview". */ }
```
Add its CSS (width `min(960px, calc(100vw - 32px))`, body `max-height: 70vh; overflow: auto`) next to it in `GraphPreviewDialog.css` or in `TaskGraph.css`, using existing CSS variables only.

