## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `GET /api/workspaces/:id/graph?tasksDir=<rel>` → 200 `{ nodes: {id,title,status:"pending"}[], edges: [from,to][], layers: string[][] }`; 400 `tasksDir is required`; 404 `no task files in <rel>` (missing, outside the workspace or empty); 404 `unknown workspace`.
- [ ] `GET /api/internal/tools` lists `open_graph` and `propose_graph` (with `tasksDir`, `spec` required).
- [ ] `open_graph` queues `{ kind: "open-graph", runId | tasksDir, node? }`; errors: `pass exactly one of runId and tasksDir`, `unknown run <id>`, `tasks folder <x> is not a folder inside the workspace`, `unknown node <n> in run <id>; nodes: …` / `unknown node <n> in <tasksDir>; nodes: …`, workspace error.
- [ ] `propose_graph` validates like `open_start_run`, queues `{ kind: "propose-graph", prefill }` and returns `Showed the graph of <tasksDir> to the user for approval. If they approve, the Start run form opens; if they reject, you'll get a message in this terminal.`
- [ ] `POST /api/agent-requests/:id/ack { result: "rejected" }` on a propose-graph request types `[graph-manager] The user rejected the graph <tasksDir>.` into its terminal via `typeWhenIdle`; `approved` and no body type nothing; another `result` → 400.
- [ ] Web: open-graph / propose-graph act at once where the terminal is on screen, else toast `<Agent> in <repo> wants to show you a graph` with Open. A run graph opens `/runs/:ws/:runId?node=<id>`; a folder graph opens the read-only preview; propose shows Approve/Reject; Approve opens the prefilled Start run drawer that sends `originTerminalId`.
- [ ] `/runs/:ws/:runId?node=<id>` selects the node in the graph and the task table and scrolls to it, showing the static view.
- [ ] Start run opened from a `start-run` request also sends `originTerminalId`.
- [ ] `npm run typecheck && npm run lint` pass and the tests below pass.

